vmdpathfinder/main.pdf

# Paper case-study: generated HOLE outputs, renders, and scratch figures.
# PDB inputs and PDFs (supp figures, scheme references) are intentionally kept.
# ONE deliberate exception: the .sph that `reproduce.sh --stage sos-sweep` times
# against. It is generated output, which this rule normally excludes - but the
# benchmark's entire meaning is "how fast do two triangulators build THE SAME
# surface", so the input must be a fixed, distributable artefact. Regenerating it
# from 9HNR.pdb instead would make it build-dependent: a new HOLE would silently
# move the published triangle counts and speedups. 47 KB, and it is the only file
# standing between a clean clone and a working `--tier1`.
# git cannot un-exclude a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so every level has to
# be re-included and then re-excluded on the way down. That is why this is verbose.

# Benchmark harness: keep the SCRIPTS and the RESULTS, never the bulk.
# Sizes at the time of writing, all of it regenerable and none of it evidence:
#   env/              772 MB  - the mdahole2 / PoreAnalyser virtualenvs
#   scratch_bench/    114 MB  - per-run scratch
#   fixtures/traj50_bare_inputs/
#                     114 MB  - 50 extracted frames, derived from the Tier-2 dcd
# `results/` (340 KB of CSVs + the figure) and `fixtures/poreanalyser_1frame/`
# (44 KB, the raw tables behind the ellipse comparison) ARE evidence and stay.
paper/benchmarks/env/
paper/benchmarks/scratch_bench/
paper/benchmarks/__pycache__/
# Any Python cache, not just that one directory. A stray
# vmdpathfinder/hole_tcl/__pycache__/*.pyc reached a commit because only the
# paper/benchmarks path was listed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
paper/benchmarks/*.log

# Editor / tool backups
*.bak
*.bak2

