# ---- Bulk data that must not be in a public repository ----------------------
# Untracked 2026-08-13. All of it is simulation input/output: large, machine-
# specific, and either regenerable or obtainable separately. Several items were
# tracked TWICE - the expanded tree and its own .tar.gz - so the repository
# carried the same 3 GB in two forms.
#
#   04_full_trajectory/             1.5 GB CAVER reference run
#   04_full_trajectory.tar.gz       481 MB - the same data again
#
# Each directory's own README.md is kept (force-added) so the tree still says
# what belonged there and how to obtain it.
#
# NOTE: untracking removes these from future checkouts but NOT from history -
# a fresh clone still pays for them. Shrinking the clone needs a history
# rewrite (git filter-repo) and a force-push, which is a destructive operation
# for anyone who has already cloned. That decision is deliberately left open.
# TRAJECTORIES ARE NOT VERSIONED. They are published with their own DOIs and a
# code repository is the wrong place to redistribute them. Download them and put
# them where paper/DATA.md says - every script looks there.
#   01_inputs/ + 04_full_trajectory/  ->  doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7234700
04_full_trajectory/
04_full_trajectory.tar.gz

